@defgroup micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated Deprecated
@brief Definitions kept for compatibility with earlier releases.

@details
The definitions in this group, and in the groups they refer to, are still
available, but the compiler reports their use, and they will be removed in
a future major release. Each one names its replacement in the deprecation
message, together with the version that deprecated it (most of them since
5.1.0).

@par Availability
The deprecated definitions are compiled only when the application defines
the macro `MICRO_OS_PLUS_MICRO_TEST_PLUS_DEPRECATED_ENABLED`, in
`micro-os-plus/project-config.h` or in
`micro-os-plus/micro-test-plus-defines.h`. Without it, the applications
that still use them fail to compile, which is a way of finding what must
be migrated.

@par Groups
The deprecated definitions are documented together with the features they
belong to:

- the overloaded comparison and logical operators, in
  @ref micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-operators, replaced by the function
  comparators and the logical functions;
- the user-defined literals and the type wrappers, in
  @ref micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-literals, replaced by the plain values
  passed to the function comparators;
- the underscore-prefixed logical functions (`_not()`, `_and()`, and `_or()`), in
  @ref micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-logical-functions, replaced by
  `negate()`, `all_of()`, and `any_of()`.

@par Other deprecated definitions
- the v5.0.1 names of the classes: `static_runner` (replaced by `runner`),
  `subtest` (replaced by `test_case`), `detail::runner_totals` (replaced by
  `counters`), and `detail::timestamps` and `detail::timestamp`, which are
  internal and not replaced;
- `runner (const char*)`, replaced by `runner()` followed by
  `add_top_suite()` (since 4.1.0);
- `runner::initialise (argc, argv, top_suite_name)`, replaced by
  `initialise (argc, argv)` followed by `add_top_suite()`;
- `runner::exit_code()`, replaced by `runner::run()`;
- `runner::suite()`, replaced by `runner::add_suite()`;
- `runner::suites_count()`, replaced by `added_suites_count()` or
  `total_suites_count()`;
- `runner::verbosity()`, and `runner::reporter()` with its `verbosity()`
  member, replaced by `runner::verbosity_level()`;
- `runner::timings()` and `test_case::timings()`, and the members of
  `detail::stopwatch` kept from the v5.0.1 timestamps, which are
  internal and not replaced;
- the `counters` members `increment_successful_checks()`,
  `increment_executed_subtests()`, `successful_checks()`,
  `executed_subtests()`, and `was_successful()`, replaced by
  `increment_passed_checks()`, `increment_executed_test_cases()`,
  `passed_checks()`, `executed_test_cases()`, and `passed()`;
- `test_case::assume()`, replaced by `test_case::require()`;
- the overloads of `test_case::expect()` and `test_case::require()` that
  accept an argument that is always true (a string literal or a function
  name), replaced by writing the condition;
- the `static_suite` constructor whose callable takes a `static_suite&`,
  replaced by a callable taking a `suite&`;
- `reflection::short_name()`, replaced by `utility::extract_file_name()`;
- the `type_traits` namespace, with the concepts and the value wrapper
  templates of v5.0.1, replaced by the `extension` namespace.

@par Migration
Build once with the deprecation warnings enabled, and rewrite each
reported use as suggested by the message. Temporarily, the warnings can be
disabled with `-Wno-deprecated-declarations`, for the applications that
build with `-Werror`.

@code{.cpp}
namespace mt = micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus;

// Deprecated.
using namespace mt::operators;
using namespace mt::literals;
t.expect (compute_answer () == 42_i) << "answer is 42";

// Replacement.
t.expect (mt::eq (compute_answer (), 42)) << "answer is 42";
@endcode
